<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8"/>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
    <base href="/"/>
    @* An SVG icon rather than an .ico: one file, sharp at every size a browser asks for, and the
       only format worth shipping to an audience running current browsers. Without it the tab
       carried the blank page glyph and the browser asked for /favicon.ico on every load and got a
       404 back. *@
    <link rel="icon" href="@Assets["favicon.svg"]" type="image/svg+xml"/>
    <ResourcePreloader/>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]"/>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["Memoria.Web.styles.css"]"/>
    @* Inline and in the head, unlike every other preference this application keeps. The rows-per-page
       choice can be put back after the page has drawn because nobody sees a table of ten become a
       table of fifty. A theme cannot: read from a file at the end of the body, the page paints white
       first and then turns dark, and that flash is on every single navigation. This is the one
       script that has to run before the first paint, so it is written where it can.

       Storage can be missing or refused outright — a private window, a browser set to block site
       data — and a reader who cannot be remembered still gets the theme their system asks for. *@
    <script>
        (function () {
            try {
                var choice = window.localStorage.getItem("memoria.theme");
                if (choice === "dark" || choice === "light") {
                    document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", choice);
                }
            } catch (e) {
            }
        })();
    </script>
    <ImportMap/>
    <HeadOutlet/>
</head>

<body>
<Routes/>
<ReconnectModal/>
<script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
@* After Blazor rather than before it: the preference has to be put back after an enhanced
   navigation as well as after a load, and that is something only Blazor can say has happened. *@
<script src="@Assets["preferences.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>